course: dictionary
lesson: 10558
title: Uncertain and what it tells us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uncertain means not sure. When you do not know what will happen, or you cannot tell which answer is right, the situation is uncertain. Look at the words around it for clues. «The trip is uncertain because of the weather» tells you that nobody knows yet whether the trip will go ahead.
explain: Uncertain can also mean not known or not decided yet. «The Buddha was an Indian teacher who lived about 2,500 years ago; his exact dates are uncertain.» Historians cannot be sure of the exact years, so the dates are not yet known for certain. Uncertain does not mean wrong. It means the answer is not fixed.
explain: Sometimes uncertain describes weather that may change suddenly. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try "not sure" in the sentence instead of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Uncertain means not sure, or not known or decided yet.
fact: Uncertain is made of "un-" (not) and "certain" (sure), so it means not certain.
fact: Uncertain can describe weather that may change suddenly.
fact: In science, results can be uncertain when measurements are not exact.
fact: "In no uncertain terms" means very clearly and firmly.
exercise: «The trip is uncertain because of the weather.» What does uncertain mean here? | Very fast | Definitely happening | *Not sure yet | Sunny and warm
exercise: «His exact dates are uncertain.» What does uncertain tell us about the dates? | They are the same as today's dates | They are very long | They are written in gold | *They are not known for sure
exercise: Find and copy the word that means not sure: «The results of the test were uncertain because the measurements were not exact.» | results | measurements | exact | *uncertain
test: Scientists say tomorrow's rain is uncertain. What does uncertain mean? | Certain to be sunny | Already finished | *Not known yet | Very loud
test: What does "in no uncertain terms" mean? | Politely | *Very clearly and firmly | Quietly and slowly | Not clear at all
exam: Why might weather be called uncertain? | Because it is made of paper | Because it is bright and clear all day | Because it is always the same | *Because it may change suddenly
